INSERT INTO "aai"."askcontent_chat_turn" ("id", "org_id", "thread_id", "ordinal", "question", "answer", "evidence", "steps", "grounded", "unsupported_reason", "answered_by", "elapsed_ms", "error", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES ('e95fa37a-a257-4c65-8136-b9a2934dde22', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', 'c11e3885-48a2-4034-ab13-15ad68c577f5', 1, 'Map survey response data into Salesforce', 'You can map survey response data into Salesforce to calculate and update average scores (NPS/CSAT/CES) for accounts based on all responses received by all contacts for that account[1]. Here is the sequence:

## 1. Create Custom Objects in Salesforce

1. Go to **Settings** → **Object Manager** → **Create a custom object**[1].
2. Create the following custom objects:
   - **Qwary Survey Response - Account**
   - **Qwary Survey Response - Contact**
   - **Qwary Survey Response - Case**
   - **Qwary Survey Response - Opportunity**
   - Edit the **Case** object as needed[1].

### Example: Create a Custom Object for Account

- Object Name: Qwary Survey Response - Account
- Add fields as required for your mapping[1].

## 2. Define Fields for Survey Data

Add the following fields to your custom objects as needed:

- **Qwary CES** (`Qwary_CES__c`): Number(18, 0) — for effort score question type[2].
- **Qwary comment** (`Qwary_comment__c`): Text Area(255) — for comment question type[2].
- **Qwary CSAT** (`Qwary_CSAT__c`): Number(18, 0) — for satisfaction question type[2].
- **Qwary emotion** (`Qwary_emotion__c`): Text(10) — for emotion question type[2].
- **Qwary NPS** (`Qwary_NPS__c`): Number(18, 0) — for NPS question type[2].
- **Qwary rating** (`Qwary_rating__c`): Number(18, 0)[2].
- **Qwary Survey Name** (`Name`): Text(80) — survey name for the received response[3].
- **Qwary Survey Response** (`Qwary_Survey_Response__c`): Rich Text Area(100000) — formatted survey response[3].

## 3. Create Event-Based Workflow in Qwary

1. Go to **Workflow** → **Create new workflow** → Enter a name → Click **Create**[8].
2. Click on **Add a Trigger** and select the survey you created for the Salesforce Case/Opportunity email campaign[8].
3. Add the task **Salesforce - Update a case/opportunity with rating and survey response in Salesforce**[8].
4. Connect your Salesforce account[8].

## 4. Connect Qwary to Salesforce

1. Log into your Salesforce account[12].
2. Go to **Settings** → **Setup**[12].
3. Go to **Platform Tools** → **App Manager** → Click **New Connected App**[12].
4. Enter the required information and click **Save**[12].
5. After saving, click on **consumer details** and save the consumer key and secret[12].
6. Use these credentials to connect Qwary to Salesforce during workflow setup[8][12].

## Consequence

Once set up, survey response data will be mapped into Salesforce, updating the relevant custom objects and fields, and calculating average scores for accounts based on all received responses[1]. This enables you to monitor customer sentiment and take action based on survey feedback directly within Salesforce[1][6].', '{"trace": {"filters": {"spaces": ["QWARY_HELP"], "doc_types": [], "labels_any": [], "principals": ["group:all-staff"], "labels_none": [], "updated_after": null, "updated_before": null}, "refusal": null, "channels": [{"top": ["https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/salesforce-workflow/map-survey-response-data-into-salesforce", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/salesforce-workflow", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/salesforce-workflow/map-survey-response-data-into-salesforce/create-event-based-salesforce-workflow", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/zendesk-workflow/map-survey-response-data-into-zendesk/event-based-zendesk-workflow", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/zendesk-workflow/map-survey-response-data-into-zendesk"], "hits": 20, "error": null, "channel": "pgp", "latency_ms": 1577.08}, {"top": ["https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/salesforce-workflow/map-survey-response-data-into-salesforce", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/zendesk-workflow/map-survey-response-data-into-zendesk", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/workflows/salesforce-workflow/import-contact-data-from-salesforce-to-qwary", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/compose-survey/enterprise-surveys", "https://help.qwary.com/product-guide/compose-survey/in-product-surveys"], "hits": 20, "error": null, "channel": "ecm", "latency_ms": 100.03}], "degraded": [], "phase_ms": {"prime": 224.8, "rerank": 0.9, "resolve": 0.3, "passages": 10.1, "candidates": 1583.1, "resolve_batch": 91.5, "embed_question": 139.5}, "synonyms": {}, "total_ms": 2052.35, "plan_hash": "pln_b2fa1043c3b0462e", "spec_json": "{\"a