 "text_yield_per_page": null}, "chunks_selected": 3}, {"title": "Rates", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/rates/?linkLoc=taskbar", "authority": "supporting", "cache_hit": true, "staleness": "unknown_age", "dropped_by": null, "parse_path": "html_trafilatura", "resolution": "resolved", "drop_detail": null, "fusion_rank": 16, "rerank_rank": null, "fusion_score": 0.013158, "rerank_score": null, "channel_ranks": {"pgp": 16}, "parse_quality": {"warnings": [], "char_count": 0, "block_count": 0, "table_count": 0, "ocr_confidence": null, "text_yield_per_page": null}, "chunks_selected": 1}], "expansions": [], "reranked_by": "pgp:cross-encoder", "cache_hit_rate": 1, "expanded_query": "", "forbidden_count": 0, "stale_index_count": 0}, "notices": ["12 cited document(s) have no parseable date; treat their currency as unverified and check the field map."], "refused": false, "citations": [{"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "span": "As an Online Banking customer, you have access to view, download, and print up to 12 months of auto loan statements. If you''d like to stop receiving paper statements in the mail, sign on to your account and select Manage delivery preferences .\n\nBefore you apply for a due date change, you''ll need to meet the following criteria:\n\n- You''ve made the first payment on your auto loan.\n\n- This is your first payment due date change. (You''re allowed one payment due date change for the entire term of the loan.)\n\n- Your account is current or no more than 10 days past due.\n\nIf you change your due date, you", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Personal Loan Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_3d993090c2ab7c74", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 2, "heading_path": ["Personal Loan Help", "You have questions, we have answers"], "rerank_score": 0.629121}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "span": "If you change your due date, your loan maturity date will be adjusted. Your monthly payment amount will remain the same.\n\nTo request a due date change, please call us at 1-800-289-8004 .\n\nSign on to your account, select your auto loan from Account Summary, and then Get payoff quote . If your payoff amount is less than $5,000, you can make an online payment to pay off your account.\n\nMail\n\n- Make your check or money order payable to Wells Fargo Auto.\n\n- Write \"Payoff\" on the memo line of the check or money order and include your 10-digit account number or 17-digit vehicle identification number (", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Personal Loan Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_f221a3b81def3465", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 2, "heading_path": ["Personal Loan Help", "You have questions, we have answers"], "rerank_score": 0.603422}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards/credit-card-faqs", "span": "You can pay your credit card bill:\n\n- By downloading the Wells Fargo Mobile \u00ae app or signing on to Wells Fargo Online. Compare your payment options\n\n- By calling the number on the back of your card.\n\n### Can I change my payment due date?\n\nYes. Sign on to the Credit Card Service Center and select Change Your Payment Due Date under Account Management . Note that the 29th through the 31st of any month will not be selectable.", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Credit Card Questions - Increase Credit Limits - Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards/credit-card-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_ca83a8c638a61c3d", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 1, "heading_path": ["Credit Card FAQs", "What should I expect after I apply online?", "How do I pay my bill?"], "rerank_score": 0.526768}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "span": "If you''d like to change your automatic payment, you''ll need to cancel the recurring schedule and then set up Autopay again. To cancel your automatic payments, sign on , select your auto loan from Account Summary, and then select Manage Autopay . Please allow at least 3 business days before the automatic payment is scheduled to withdraw.\n\nAs an Online Banking customer, you have access to view, download, and print up to 12 months of auto loan statements. If you''d like to stop receiving paper statements in the mail, sign on to your account and select Manage delivery preferences .\n\nBefore you appl", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Personal Loan Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_a58d027db38525e3", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 2, "heading_path": ["Personal Loan Help", "You have questions, we have answers"], "rerank_score": 0.546742}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "span": "Before you apply for a due date change, you''ll need to meet the following criteria:\n\n- You''ve made the first payment on your auto loan.\n\n- This is your first payment due date change. (You''re allowed one payment due date change for the entire term of the loan.)\n\n- Your account is current or no more than 10 days past due.\n\nIf you change your due date, your loan maturity date will be adjusted. Your monthly payment amount will remain the same.\n\nTo request a due date change, please call us at 1-800-289-8004 .\n\nIf you''re making your monthly payment that''s currently due , it will be applied in the fo", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Auto loans FAQs | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_6bcc5a2f25cf1828", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 8, "heading_path": ["Auto loan FAQs", "Auto loan payments"], "rerank_score": 0.641759}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "span": "Note: For stop payments on recurring debit card transactions call us at 1-800-TO-WELLS ( 1-800-869-3557 ) or speak to a banker at any Wells Fargo branch.", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Checking and Savings Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_cf81b0fca25bc25e", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 3, "heading_path": ["Checking and Savings Help", "You have questions, we have answers", "How do I place a stop payment on a check or pre-authorized payment (ACH Automated Clearing House) item?"], "rerank_score": 0.404639}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards", "span": "You\u2019ll need to continue to make payments as usual except for amounts in dispute. If you\u2019re enrolled in automatic payment or Overdraft Protection, these services may be temporarily unavailable for up to 72 hours while we set up your new account.", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Credit Card Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_5e8730e76fef1412", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 4, "heading_path": ["Credit Card Help", "Top Questions", "What should I do about payments if my card is lost or stolen?"], "rerank_score": 0.402435}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "span": "If you''re making your monthly payment that''s past due (after the due date), it will be applied in the following order:\n\n- Accrued interest\n\n- Principal\n\nNote: Fees and other charges won''t automatically be paid if you''re past due.\n\nRefer to your monthly statement to see how your payment was applied to interest, principal, fees, and other charges.\n\nNo, we can''t accommodate checks with future dates (post-dated checks). If you mail a postdated check, it will be processed on the date it''s received. You can schedule a payment for a future date online or by phone.\n\nThere may be a fee for missing a pa", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Auto loans FAQs | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_45a804a9a9e6e33e", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 8, "heading_path": ["Auto loan FAQs", "Auto loan payments"], "rerank_score": 0.519324}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "span": "Grace periods vary from state to state, so please review your loan contract for information about the grace period and late fees. If you''re unable to find your loan contract, please call us for more information or to request a copy.\n\nIf your payment is 30 or more days late, it may show up on your credit report as a late payment. The degree to which a late payment affects your credit score can depend on things like how many days past due the payment is, how recently you''ve been past due, and how frequently you\u2019ve made late payments.\n\nReview your credit report so you know where you stand. Free c", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Auto loans FAQs | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_ec0d43d9d4dc37ca", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 8, "heading_path": ["Auto loan FAQs", "Payment challenges"], "rerank_score": 0.465163}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "span": "- Review your statements for automatic transactions and cancel them by contacting the merchant(s).\n\n- When you have a previously authorized transaction, such as ATM and debit card transactions, account transfers, and Wells Fargo Online Bill Pay transactions presented for payment and your account doesn''t have enough money, we will pay the item(s) into overdraft and an overdraft fee may be assessed . Please refer to the Deposit Account Agreement and Consumer Fee and Information Schedule for more information.\n\n- When checks and preauthorized automatic payments (ACH) are presented for payment and ", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Checking and Savings Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_eadc3067a74396e9", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 3, "heading_path": ["Checking and Savings Help", "You have questions, we have answers", "How do I close a checking or savings account?"], "rerank_score": 0.383105}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "span": "Follow these steps for setting up Direct Deposit .\n\n### When will my deposit be credited to my account?\n\nIf you make your deposit on a business day before the cutoff time displayed at the banking location, ATM, or on the Wells Fargo Mobile \u00ae app, we will generally credit the deposit to your account the same business day. If you make your deposit after the cutoff time or on a non-business day, we will credit it to your account on the next business day.\n\n- Business days are Monday through Friday, except for federal holidays.\n\n- Cutoff times are displayed in all locations. The cutoff time for mos", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Checking and Savings Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_6a11939de131614e", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 3, "heading_path": ["Checking and Savings Help", "You have questions, we have answers", "How do I set up Direct Deposit?"], "rerank_score": 0.382036}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/home-lending", "span": "We can help you understand your options if you are facing payment challenges. Call 1-800-678-7986 .\n\n## Tools and Calculators\n\n- Get prequalified\n\n### Call Us\n\nGive Us Feedback", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Home Lending Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/home-lending", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_d0c1752e51064f66", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 7, "heading_path": ["Home Lending Help", "Top Questions", "Who do I contact if I am having trouble paying my mortgage?"], "rerank_score": 0.397221}], "conflicts": [], "followups": [{"because": "these passages", "question": "What criteria do I need before I apply for a due date change?"}, {"because": "these passages", "question": "Will my loan maturity date be adjusted if I change my due date?"}, {"because": "these passages", "question": "Will my monthly payment amount remain the same?"}, {"because": "these passages", "question": "Can I change my payment due date on a credit card?"}], "answered_by": {"cited": [1, 2, 5], "model": "gpt-4.1-2025-04-14", "grounded": true, "provider": "langchain"}, "refusal_reason": null}'::jsonb, '[{"ms": "under 1 ms", "name": "compile", "label": "Compiling scope and permissions", "detail": "plan pln_7301c26d3481aaad", "status": "ok"}, {"ms": "884 ms", "name": "candidates", "label": "Searching the index and the store", "detail": "pgp 16, ecm 0", "status": "ok"}, {"ms": "248 ms", "name": "resolve", "label": "Resolving candidates against the store", "detail": "16 candidates, 0 stale, 0 forbidden", "status": 