atements in the mail, sign on to your account and select Manage delivery preferences .\n\nBefore you appl", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Personal Loan Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_a58d027db38525e3", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 1, "heading_path": ["Personal Loan Help", "You have questions, we have answers"], "rerank_score": 0.575783}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "span": "- Review your statements for automatic transactions and cancel them by contacting the merchant(s).\n\n- When you have a previously authorized transaction, such as ATM and debit card transactions, account transfers, and Wells Fargo Online Bill Pay transactions presented for payment and your account doesn''t have enough money, we will pay the item(s) into overdraft and an overdraft fee may be assessed . Please refer to the Deposit Account Agreement and Consumer Fee and Information Schedule for more information.\n\n- When checks and preauthorized automatic payments (ACH) are presented for payment and ", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Checking and Savings Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_eadc3067a74396e9", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 2, "heading_path": ["Checking and Savings Help", "You have questions, we have answers", "How do I close a checking or savings account?"], "rerank_score": 0.565484}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "span": "As an Online Banking customer, you have access to view, download, and print up to 12 months of auto loan statements. If you''d like to stop receiving paper statements in the mail, sign on to your account and select Manage delivery preferences .\n\nBefore you apply for a due date change, you''ll need to meet the following criteria:\n\n- You''ve made the first payment on your auto loan.\n\n- This is your first payment due date change. (You''re allowed one payment due date change for the entire term of the loan.)\n\n- Your account is current or no more than 10 days past due.\n\nIf you change your due date, you", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Personal Loan Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_3d993090c2ab7c74", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 1, "heading_path": ["Personal Loan Help", "You have questions, we have answers"], "rerank_score": 0.541868}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "span": "Note: For stop payments on recurring debit card transactions call us at 1-800-TO-WELLS ( 1-800-869-3557 ) or speak to a banker at any Wells Fargo branch.", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Checking and Savings Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_cf81b0fca25bc25e", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 2, "heading_path": ["Checking and Savings Help", "You have questions, we have answers", "How do I place a stop payment on a check or pre-authorized payment (ACH Automated Clearing House) item?"], "rerank_score": 0.541737}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "span": "Wells Fargo Auto PO Box 51963 Los Angeles, CA 90051-6263\n\n- Online bill pay - Your financial institution may offer a bill pay service. Please use your 10-digit Wells Fargo Auto account number and the mailing address Wells Fargo Auto, PO Box 51963, Los Angeles, CA 90051-6263 for the payee information.\n\n- MoneyGram \u00ae - Include your 10-digit Wells Fargo Auto account number and Receive Code 1815 . Please note: Third-party fees may apply.\n\n- Western Union \u00ae - Include your 10-digit Wells Fargo Auto account number, Western Union City Code CATX , and State Code TX . Please note: Third-party fees may a", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Personal Loan Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_388b9bec9ac5fed7", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 1, "heading_path": ["Personal Loan Help", "You have questions, we have answers"], "rerank_score": 0.508262}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "span": "Before you apply for a due date change, you''ll need to meet the following criteria:\n\n- You''ve made the first payment on your auto loan.\n\n- This is your first payment due date change. (You''re allowed one payment due date change for the entire term of the loan.)\n\n- Your account is current or no more than 10 days past due.\n\nIf you change your due date, your loan maturity date will be adjusted. Your monthly payment amount will remain the same.\n\nTo request a due date change, please call us at 1-800-289-8004 .\n\nIf you''re making your monthly payment that''s currently due , it will be applied in the fo", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Auto loans FAQs | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_6bcc5a2f25cf1828", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 6, "heading_path": ["Auto loan FAQs", "Auto loan payments"], "rerank_score": 0.546557}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "span": "- Accounts with a zero balance will continue to be charged applicable fees (like the monthly service fee) until you request to close your account.\n\n- Any recurring payments or withdrawals (such as bill payments and debit card payments) from your account need to be cancelled before your request to close; otherwise, they may be returned unpaid. The payee or merchant may charge fees for returned items.\n\nHow do I close a CD (Time account)?\n\n- Call us at 1-800-TO-WELLS ( 1-800-869-3557 )\n\n- Visit a Wells Fargo branch near you.\n\n- Or complete the Account Closure or Partial Withdrawal Request form (P", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Checking and Savings Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/checking-savings", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_0dcce37502c3168e", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 2, "heading_path": ["Checking and Savings Help", "You have questions, we have answers", "How do I close a checking or savings account?"], "rerank_score": 0.471894}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards", "span": "You\u2019ll need to continue to make payments as usual except for amounts in dispute. If you\u2019re enrolled in automatic payment or Overdraft Protection, these services may be temporarily unavailable for up to 72 hours while we set up your new account.", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Credit Card Help | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_5e8730e76fef1412", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 3, "heading_path": ["Credit Card Help", "Top Questions", "What should I do about payments if my card is lost or stolen?"], "rerank_score": 0.479262}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "span": "You have many options for making payments.\n\nSet up automatic payments With automatic payments, your payment is debited monthly from your checking or savings account. To set up automatic payments, sign on , select your auto loan from Account Summary, and then select Set up Autopay . You can also call us at 1-800-289-8004 or download the automatic loan payments authorization (PDF) , complete the form, and return by mail or fax.\n\nPay by phone Call 1-800-289-8004 , 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, to use our automated system.\n\nPay by mail Make your check or money order payable to Wells Fargo Auto. B", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Auto loans FAQs | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_d5df1db5114b4d44", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 6, "heading_path": ["Auto loan FAQs", "Auto loan payments"], "rerank_score": 0.541222}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "span": "Other ways to pay\n\n- Online bill pay - Your financial institution may offer a bill pay service. Please use your 10-digit Wells Fargo Auto account number and the mailing address Wells Fargo Auto, PO Box 51963, Los Angeles, CA 90051-6263 for the payee information .\n\n- MoneyGram\u00ae - Include your 10-digit Wells Fargo Auto account number and Receive Code 1815 . Please note: Third-party fees may apply.\n\n- Western Union\u00ae - Include your 10-digit Wells Fargo Auto account number, Western Union City Code CATX , and State Code TX . Please note: Third-party fees may apply.\n\nTo set up automatic payments, sig", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Auto loans FAQs | Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/loans/auto-loans-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_83138e20c4aafa51", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 6, "heading_path": ["Auto loan FAQs", "Auto loan payments"], "rerank_score": 0.524953}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards/credit-card-faqs", "span": "You can pay your credit card bill:\n\n- By downloading the Wells Fargo Mobile \u00ae app or signing on to Wells Fargo Online. Compare your payment options\n\n- By calling the number on the back of your card.\n\n### Can I change my payment due date?\n\nYes. Sign on to the Credit Card Service Center and select Change Your Payment Due Date under Account Management . Note that the 29th through the 31st of any month will not be selectable.", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Credit Card Questions - Increase Credit Limits - Wells Fargo", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/credit-cards/credit-card-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_ca83a8c638a61c3d", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 4, "heading_path": ["Credit Card FAQs", "What should I expect after I apply online?", "How do I pay my bill?"], "rerank_score": 0.4542}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/online-banking/zelle-faqs", "span": "We recommend that you only use Zelle \u00ae to send and receive money with people and small businesses you know and trust. Always remember to carefully verify your recipient\u2019s email address or U.S. mobile number, or Zelle \u00ae tag before you send money.\n\nOnce a payment has been sent, it can\u2019t be reversed.\n\nWe\u2019ll email you and send you a secure inbox message whenever you schedule a payment or make changes to a payment. You\u2019ll also get email notifications if a payment fails or is canceled. Make sure the information in your profile is up to date so you can get those messages.\n\nWells Fargo may also send y", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Send and Receive Money with Zelle \u2013 Frequently Asked Questions", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/online-banking/zelle-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_5e975142beda97b2", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 13, "heading_path": ["Zelle \u00ae Questions"], "rerank_score": 0.470462}], "conflicts