INSERT INTO "aai"."askcontent_chat_turn" ("id", "org_id", "thread_id", "ordinal", "question", "answer", "evidence", "steps", "grounded", "unsupported_reason", "answered_by", "elapsed_ms", "error", "created_at", "updated_at") VALUES ('0fbeaee6-f30f-4d77-af80-37cb54c3168f', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', 'c864690b-fe1a-4a54-8fef-da6a75475e4e', 1, 'How do I make a payment immediately or schedule a payment up to 30 days in advance?', 'You can make an immediate payment or schedule a payment up to 30 days in advance using Zelle® if your recipient is an enrolled Zelle® user[3].

## To Make an Immediate Payment

1. Set up your payment in Zelle® and send it to an enrolled Zelle® user[4].
2. Same-day Zelle® payments are sent immediately and, if the recipient is already enrolled, the payment is sent directly to their bank account and cannot be canceled[4].

## To Schedule a Payment Up to 30 Days in Advance

1. When setting up your payment in Zelle®, turn on the **Repeat payment** toggle[3].
2. Use the calendar to schedule a single payment for a future date, up to a year in advance[3].
   - You can only send a scheduled or repeating payment to enrolled Zelle® users[3].
3. Go to **Scheduled** to see all your future payments, including one-time or repeating series[3].
   - Once a scheduled payment is complete, it will move to **Activity** with other completed payments[3].

## Additional Details

- Payments can be scheduled up to a year in advance, not just 30 days, but 30 days is within this window[3].
- You can view or manage your scheduled payments in the **Scheduled** section[3].
- Only enrolled Zelle® users can receive scheduled or repeating payments[3].

