on.\n\nFor additional help, you can call Wells Fargo Online Customer Service at 1-800-956-4442 , 24 hours a day, 7 days a week.\n\nSame-day Zelle payments are sent immediately. If your recipient has already enrolled with Zelle \u00ae , the payment is sent directly to their bank account and cannot be canceled. Keep in mind that Zelle \u00ae transactions are not covered by the same protections as credit card and debit card payments.\n\nIf the payment is still pending because your recipi", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Send and Receive Money with Zelle \u2013 Frequently Asked Questions", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/online-banking/zelle-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_ef1ec42f872c4fbb", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 1, "heading_path": ["Zelle \u00ae Questions"], "rerank_score": 1}, {"url": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/online-banking/zelle-faqs", "span": "When you\u2019re setting up your payment, turn on the Repeat payment toggle. This will allow you to set up a payment series or use the calendar to schedule a single payment sometime in the future.\n\nPayments can be scheduled up to a year in advance. Keep in mind you can only send a scheduled or repeating payment to enrolled Zelle \u00ae users.\n\nGo to Scheduled to see all of your future payments, including one-time payments or any repeating series. Once each payment is complete, it will move to Activity , along with other completed payments.\n\nYou can also access canceled payments in Scheduled, for up to t", "owner": "crawler", "space": "WELLSFARGO_HELP_CENTER", "title": "Send and Receive Money with Zelle \u2013 Frequently Asked Questions", "doc_id": "https://www.wellsfargo.com/help/online-banking/zelle-faqs", "labels": ["crawled"], "chunk_id": "chk_5ad9d57580c161de", "authority": "supporting", "staleness": "unknown_age", "updated_at": null, "fusion_rank": 1, "heading_path": ["Zelle \u00ae 